261:     - Identify the anchor sprite (contains the marker pixel) and the remaining pieces.
262:     - Rotate the anchor so the marker pixel lands at position (0,0) of the output.
263:     - Pack all remaining pieces (allowing 90° rotations) to tile a complete rectangle with no gaps.
264: 
265:     Key insight: The lone marker pixel picks the anchor and fixes the output orientation — it must sit at the top-left corner.
266:     """
